# Understand Anything incremental in {{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/

Before any action with Understand Anything in this repo, read:

- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (or `AGENTS.md`)
- the architecture doc that documents this mechanism in this project (if any)

## Blocking rule

The product's main graph uses `PROJECT_ROOT={{ harness_understand_apps_root }}`, but the real Git root is the repo root. Therefore, the incremental list of changed files must be relative to `{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/`.

Use:

```bash
bash .harness/lib/understand-apps-changed-files.sh
```

or, manually:

```bash
LAST=$(node -e "const fs=require('fs'); const m=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/.understand-anything/meta.json','utf8')); process.stdout.write(m.gitCommitHash)")
git diff --relative={{ harness_understand_apps_root }} "$LAST"..HEAD --name-only -- {{ harness_understand_apps_root }} | rg -v '^\.understand-anything/'
```

The reference hash of the current graph **is not a constant** — always read it from
`{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/.understand-anything/meta.json` (field `gitCommitHash`,
the `LAST=` command above). Do not hardcode a memorized hash in the doc/skill: it desyncs on
every incremental `/understand` (a real finding from the donor harness — the hash cited in a
static doc has already drifted from the real graph more than once).

## Forbidden

Do not use:

```bash
git diff <lastCommitHash>..HEAD --name-only
git -C {{ harness_understand_apps_root }} diff <lastCommitHash>..HEAD --name-only
```

These commands emit `{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/api/...`, but `compute-batches` expects `api/...` when the analyzed project is `{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/`.

## Checklist

1. Confirm that `{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/.understand-anything/meta.json` exists.
2. Generate changed files with `.harness/lib/understand-apps-changed-files.sh`.
3. Validate that the list does not contain `{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/`, `.claude/`, `.agents/`, `docs/`, `scripts/` or other root paths.
4. Run incremental without `--full`.
5. If updating the dashboard, remember it reads `{{ harness_understand_apps_root }}/.understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json`.
